note('Weight-space check confirmed sink interpretation: blocks 3–8 V bias and normalized column 62 are nearly antiparallel (cos −0.97 to −0.99); cancel at a positive RMS-scaled value of ~20–23. Query-bias/key-column couplings support sink affinity. B_d rank-one phase in blocks 2 and 21 nearly exactly matches the sign of A on the giant anti-aligned SwiGLU neuron, so those changes mainly target sink behavior. A plain negative top early d vector would apply it to all tokens incorrectly. For ordinary tokens, G/U sketches consistently identify a mean axis +570 −208 −262. Analytic Gaussian moment contractions (not block evaluations) show increasing signed MLP edits late. Independently, delta-O applied to learned value bias in blocks 17,20,21,23 coherently raises “only/minor” and/or end-of-answer and suppresses “If”, newline, continuation. This offers an interpretable signed correction, not a chosen SVD sign.')